[h1]Project Vigilance: Overland Incursions[/h1]
[b]Replaces instantaneous map-edge teleportation with physical overland planetary transit, dynamic multi-vector staging, realistic transit ETAs, sensory sight horizons, classic 3-tier Haze of War, and tactical ground interception.[/b]
No high-tech requirements. Zero prerequisites. Safe to add mid-save.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Key Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Real-Time Planetary Transit:[/b] Raids, trade caravans, and visitors spawn at genuine world origin settlements or wilderness staging camps and march across the globe in real time.
[*] [b]Tactical Ground Interception & Forward Ambush (New in v0.3):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Intercept approaching hostile incursions directly on the global hex grid before they reach your colony.
    [*] Right-click commands on detected incursions: [i]Intercept & Engage[/i], [i]Hail & Trade[/i], or [i]Warn Away / Turn Back[/i].
    [*] Stalk unaware enemy columns or launch daring night ambushes while hostile warbands are camped asleep.
    [*] Intercepting caravans dynamically adjust course with predictive pursuit vectoring as their quarry moves.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Retreat Lifecycle, Pursuit & Kidnap Recovery (New in v0.3):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Fleeing raiders physically retreat across the world map with wounds, carried loot, and captured colonists intact.
    [*] Overland physiology: wounded marchers bleed, heal, self-tend with carried medicine, or suffer exhaustion.
    [*] Intercept retreating kidnappers on the road to rescue captured colonists before they reach home territory—or mount a base assault on their stronghold to liberate prisoners from settlement incarceration!
    [*] Threat-aware tactical retreats: fleeing colonists evaluate visible enemies, turrets, and fire exposure across all map boundaries to pick the safest evacuation corridor.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Evacuated Colony Hierarchy & Track Pursuit (New in v0.3):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Hostile forces reaching an evacuated player colony or abandoned settlement don't disappear into thin air.
    [*] Raiders execute a 3-tier tactical hierarchy: search for tracks and launch dynamic hot pursuit after fleeing player caravans, divert toward nearby secondary outposts, or ransack the vacant site and march home.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Night Owl & Schedule-Aware Caravaning (New in v0.3):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Caravans respect colonist traits and timetable schedules rather than enforcing rigid 22:00–06:00 sleep locks.
    [*] Pure Night Owl squads camp during the day (11:00–18:00) and march through the night with zero optical darkness penalties.
    [*] Mixed squads march by majority shift while keeping the other on camp watch—granting 24/7 daytime visibility.
    [*] Set custom sleep shifts or force-march through rest hours via the colonist [i]Schedule[/i] tab.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Pack Animal Cargo & Roadside Trading (New in v0.3):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Trade goods and provisions are carried in pack animal inventories across all battle maps and transits (no floor-dumping).
    [*] Barter with friendly travelling merchants directly on the road without duplicating stock upon colony arrival.
    [*] Trader loss lifecycle: surviving escort guards execute tactical withdrawals if their merchant falls.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Classic 3-Tier Haze of War:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] [i]Shrouded:[/i] Pitch-black mask over unmapped planetary tiles.
    [*] [i]Obscured:[/i] Surveyed world geography and settlements remain visible, but active incursions are hidden outside sensor coverage.
    [*] [i]Monitored:[/i] Full live sensory visibility projected by your colonies, outposts, and traveling caravans.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Watertight Information Security & X-COM Tracking IDs:[/b] Approaching forces outside your immediate sight lines are designated with persistent tracking numbers ([i]Contact-1[/i], [i]Contact-2[/i] or [i]Approaching Strangers #1[/i] for tribals). Originating faction, threat points, and route overlays remain classified until scouted.
[*] [b]Dynamic Nighttime & Sleep Simulation:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Visual detection horizons drop by 50% during local planetary darkness.
    [*] Settlement lookouts collapse to a tight perimeter when all conscious colonists are asleep in bed.
    [*] Biological warbands and trade caravans stop and make camp between 22:00 and 06:00 local solar time, while tireless Mechanoid and Anomaly incursions march 24/7.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Dynamic Staging & Multi-Vector Raids:[/b] Incursions originate from nearby settlements or procedurally staged wilderness camps, converging on your base from diverse tactical vectors.
[*] [b]Realistic ETAs & Terrain Costs:[/b] Overland speeds reflect real biomes, roads, rivers, and mountains. Incursions take anywhere from 12 in-game hours to several days to arrive.
[*] [b]Tactical Map Rendering & IFF Markers:[/b] Crimson red markers for hostile incursions; cyan markers for friendly and neutral caravans, combining marching silhouettes with high-contrast faction crests.
[*] [b]Interactive World Telemetry:[/b] Click detected incursions to inspect speed, distance, live ETA, and combat threat ratings.
[*] [b]Configurable In-Game Settings:[/b] Customise settlement sight range, caravan vision, night reduction penalties, and march speed multipliers directly in Mod Options.
[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility & Performance[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]DLC Compatibility:[/b] 100% compatible with the base game, as well as Royalty, Ideology, Biotech, Anomaly, and Odyssey.
[*] [b]Save Games:[/b] Safe to add to existing saves. Safe to remove (any in-flight world incursions will simply disband cleanly).
[*] [b]Era Agnostic:[/b] Fits seamlessly into neolithic, medieval, industrial, or spacer playthroughs.
[*] [b]Performance:[/b] Zero-allocation spatial bitmasks and time-sliced 3D mesh layers guarantee buttery-smooth 60 FPS panning with zero TPS impact.
[/list]
[h2]Recommended Load Order[/h2]
[olist]
[*] Harmony
[*] Core
[*] All Official DLCs (optional)
[*] [b]Project Vigilance - Overland Incursions[/b]
[/olist]
[hr][/hr]
